{
 "note": "The Ship Inn, 8 Albert Street, Busselton: the two-storey 1928 hotel (J. L. Ochiltree) on the south-east corner of Albert and West Streets, on the site of George Guerrier's 1847 Ship Inn. From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), 2019 street photos and the inHerit record. White-painted brick, pale grey hipped corrugated roofs, a deep cantilevered first-floor balcony along Albert Street with a dark slatted balustrade, its roof carried out from the main roof, and red THE SHIP INN banners on it. The limestone stables wing to the east is its own spec (ship_inn_stables.json) because it sits square to Albert Street, not to West Street. Signs are plain lettering, no logos. Metres: x left to right as seen from Albert Street (east to west), y back from the balcony edge (south).",
